  "statement": "A grid has `h` rows and `w` columns; each cell is free (`.`) or blocked (`#`). Starting at the top-left cell you may only move one step right or one step down, never onto a blocked cell. Count the paths to the bottom-right cell, modulo `1 000 000 007`. If the start or the end is blocked the answer is `0`.\n\n**Input.** First line: `h` and `w`. Then `h` lines of `w` characters each.\n\n**Output.** One integer, the number of paths modulo `1 000 000 007`.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ h, w ≤ 120 in this browser version (intended solution works at 5000 × 5000 with O(w) memory)"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 2000,
  "hints": [
    "Let dp[i][j] be the number of ways to reach cell (i, j). Which two neighbours can you have come from?",
    "dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j] + dp[i][j-1] when the cell is free, and 0 when it is blocked. Remember to take the modulus after every addition.",
    "Row i only needs row i-1. Keep a single array of length w: when you process cell j in row i, dp[j] still holds the value from row i-1 (the cell above), and dp[j-1] has already been updated for row i (the cell to the left). Memory drops from O(h * w) to O(w)."
  ],
  "editorial": "The recurrence is `dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j] + dp[i][j-1]` for free cells (0 for blocked), with `dp[0][0] = 1` if the start is free. A full table needs `h * w` integers: at `5000 x 5000` that is 25 million entries, about 100 MB with 32-bit ints, over a typical 256 MB limit once you add the input grid.\n\nBecause each row depends only on the previous one, use one array `row` of length `w`. Processing row `i` left to right, `row[j]` before the update is the cell above, and `row[j-1]` after its update is the cell to the left, so `row[j] = (row[j] + row[j-1]) % MOD` for a free cell and `row[j] = 0` for a blocked cell. Time stays `O(h * w)`, memory is `O(w)`.\n\nEdge cases tested: blocked start, blocked end, a single row, a single cell.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n^2)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\nMOD = 10**9 + 7\nlines = sys.stdin.read().split()\nh, w = int(lines[0]), int(lines[1])\ngrid = lines[2:2 + h]\n# one array of length w is enough\n",
    "javascript": "const [h, w] = readLine().split(' ').map(Number);\nconst MOD = 1000000007;\n// read h lines; keep a single row array\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int h, w;\n    cin >> h >> w;\n    const int MOD = 1000000007;\n    // read h strings; keep a single row array\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(new String(System.in.readAllBytes()));\n        int h = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        int w = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        final int MOD = 1_000_000_007;\n        // read h tokens (the rows); keep a single row array\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\nMOD = 10**9 + 7\nparts = sys.stdin.read().split()\nh, w = int(parts[0]), int(parts[1])\ngrid = parts[2:2 + h]\nrow = [0] * w\nfor i in range(h):\n    g = grid[i]\n    for j in range(w):\n        if g[j] == '#':\n            row[j] = 0\n        elif i == 0 and j == 0:\n            row[j] = 1\n        else:\n            left = row[j - 1] if j > 0 else 0\n            row[j] = (row[j] + left) % MOD\nprint(row[w - 1] % MOD)\n",
    "javascript": "const [h, w] = readLine().split(' ').map(Number);\nconst MOD = 1000000007;\nconst row = new Array(w).fill(0);\nfor (let i = 0; i < h; i++) {\n  const g = readLine().trim();\n  for (let j = 0; j < w; j++) {\n    if (g[j] === '#') row[j] = 0;\n    else if (i === 0 && j === 0) row[j] = 1;\n    else row[j] = (row[j] + (j > 0 ? row[j - 1] : 0)) % MOD;\n  }\n}\nconsole.log(String(row[w - 1] % MOD));\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int h, w;\n    cin >> h >> w;\n    const int MOD = 1000000007;\n    vector<int> row(w, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i < h; i++) {\n        string g;\n        cin >> g;\n        for (int j = 0; j < w; j++) {\n            if (g[j] == '#') row[j] = 0;\n            else if (i == 0 && j == 0) row[j] = 1;\n            else row[j] = (row[j] + (j > 0 ? row[j - 1] : 0)) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << row[w - 1] % MOD << endl;\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(new String(System.in.readAllBytes()));\n        int h = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        int w = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        final int MOD = 1_000_000_007;\n        int[] row = new int[w];\n        for (int i = 0; i < h; i++) {\n            String g = st.nextToken();\n            for (int j = 0; j < w; j++) {\n                if (g.charAt(j) == '#') row[j] = 0;\n                else if (i == 0 && j == 0) row[j] = 1;\n                else row[j] = (row[j] + (j > 0 ? row[j - 1] : 0)) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(row[w - 1] % MOD);\n    }\n}\n"
  },
